  "query_preview": "(Saturday through Tuesday)... \nCooling trends will continue into this weekend with as a fairly \ndeep trough will likely build down the West Coast. Limited to no \nheat impacts are expected for the first time in awhile by this \nSunday with highs generally in the 70s and 80s, hottest towards \nthe interior.\n\nThe National Hurricane Center shows the remnant low from what was\nHurricane Rachel approaching the northern Baja of California this\nweekend and will likely pass through this region by early next \nweek. If the storm tracks closer to the region (40-50 percent \nchance), generally light showers within a tropical airmass are \npossible Sunday and Monday in particular, focused south and east \nof Orange County and across the mountains.\n\nGusty onshore winds may approach advisory levels for favored \npasses mountains and deserts Sunday or Monday.",
